        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "That confirms the upload failed entirely, not just paused.\n\nMost common causes for MP4 upload failures like this:\n\n- File is too large\n- Corrupted video export\n- Special characters/file naming issue\n- Browser/Drive cache glitch\n- Temporary Google Drive issue\n- Weak or interrupted internet\n\nFastest fixes:\n\n1. Rename the file\nChange `CO088.MP4` \u2192 `video.mp4`\n\n2. Try opening the MP4 locally\nDouble-click it and confirm it actually plays all the way through.  \nIf it won\u2019t play, the export is corrupted.\n\n3. Re-export/compress it\nIf it\u2019s huge (like several GB), compress it first using:\n- HandBrake\n- CapCut export\n- VLC convert/save\n\n4. Upload a different file\nTest with a tiny image or short video.  \nIf that uploads fine, the problem is the MP4 itself.\n\n5. Try drag-and-drop directly into Drive\nInstead of using the upload picker.\n\n6. Use Chrome only\nDrive uploads fail more often in Safari/Edge sometimes.\n\n7. Clear stuck upload state\n- Refresh Drive\n- Close all Drive tabs\n- Reopen and upload again\n\nIf you want, tell me:\n- approximate file size\n- where the video came from (iPhone, CapCut, Adobe, Canva, etc.)\n- whether it plays locally\n\n\u2026and I can pinpoint the exact issue fast."
          ]
        },
