    "e3062610-f5cb-4bb6-93fe-ab6b470a90d8": {
      "id": "e3062610-f5cb-4bb6-93fe-ab6b470a90d8",
      "message": {
        "author": {
          "name": null,
          "role": "assistant"
        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "No, it looks stuck.\n\nIf it has been sitting on \u201cStarting upload\u2026\u201d for hours with the spinning circle and no progress bar movement, the upload likely failed or froze before it even began transferring.\n\nTry these in order:\n\n1. Cancel the upload  \n2. Refresh the browser tab completely  \n3. Re-upload the file  \n4. If it freezes again:\n   - Rename the file to something simple like `video1.mp4`\n   - Check the file size (very large MP4s can hang)\n   - Try Chrome or an incognito window\n   - Make sure Google Drive desktop sync is not conflicting\n   - Restart the browser\n\nAlso, that icon looks like Google Drive upload from the web UI. Sometimes Drive gets stuck if:\n- internet briefly dropped\n- browser memory overloaded\n- Drive session expired\n- the video is still open/exporting elsewhere\n\nIf you want, I can also help you:\n- reduce/compress the MP4 size\n- diagnose why that specific video won\u2019t upload\n- show fastest settings for large video uploads to Drive/cloud storage"
          ]
        },
